+The global instruction fetch behavior is controlled by `no_x` bit in the `HWCFG3` register:
 
-* `chk_x = 0`: The IOPMP does not perform instruction fetch permission checking
-* `chk_x = 1`, `no_x = 0`: The IOPMP performs instruction fetch permission checking based on entry-level rules
-* `chk_x = 1`, `no_x = 1`: The IOPMP denies all instruction fetch transactions
+* `no_x = 0`: The IOPMP performs instruction fetch permission checking based on entry-level rules
+* `no_x = 1`: The IOPMP denies all instruction fetch transactions and reports them with error type "not hit any rule" (0x05)
 
